From 8b6e0af5f8e8c8f0e4b4a4f2a2b0f5b1a1d2c3e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guo Yunhe <i@guoyunhe.me>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 18:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Link the GLEW imported target instead of GLEW_LIBRARIES

CMake's FindGLEW module prefers GLEW's own CMake package when the distribution
ships one, which openSUSE does. With CMake 4 that path reads Windows only
imported properties (IMPORTED_IMPLIB_*), so the legacy GLEW_LIBRARIES variable
ends up as the literal "GLEW_LIBRARY-NOTFOUND" and generation then fails with:

    The following variables are used in this project, but they are set to NOTFOUND.
    Please set them or make sure they are set and tested correctly in the CMake files:
    GLEW_LIBRARY
        linked by target "anura" in directory ...

The GLEW::GLEW imported target is right in both cases, GLEW's own CMake package
provides it and FindGLEW creates it as well when it has to search for the
libraries itself, so link that instead. The linux-steam build already does it
this way.

--- a/buildsystem/linux-dynamic/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/buildsystem/linux-dynamic/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -239,7 +239,9 @@
     "${Boost_LIBRARIES}"
     "${ZLIB_LIBRARIES}"
     "${OPENGL_LIBRARIES}"
-    "${GLEW_LIBRARIES}"
+    # GLEW::GLEW is the imported target, "${GLEW_LIBRARIES}" is set to a
+    # NOTFOUND value when GLEW provides its own CMake package
+    GLEW::GLEW
     "${FREETYPE_LIBRARIES}"
     "${SDL2_LIBRARY}"
     "${SDL2_IMAGE_LIBRARIES}"
-- 
